<section id="story">
<h2>Brand story</h2>
<p>Eclipse is W.W. Wood Products' frameless full-access answer to the demand for <strong>European-style cabinetry at a domestic price point</strong>. Officially branded "eclipse by Shiloh," it's built in the same Dudley, Missouri factory as Shiloh, by the same craftspeople, with the same hardware program — but engineered around a contemporary frameless box rather than a face-frame.</p>

<p>Eclipse is American-made frameless, ships in six weeks, and rides on the same WW Wood delivery as a Shiloh order in the same house. It's also the <em>only</em> WW Wood brand that offers the specialty-materials library — high-gloss acrylic, matte velvet acrylic, gloss HPL, matte noir HPL (RAUVISIO), wood-grain HPL, TFL, natural oak/walnut veneers, and a new PV polymer laminate.</p>

<p>On the <strong>Metropolitan</strong> slab door, Eclipse delivers <strong>automatic grain matching across every material — wood, veneer, and laminate — at no upcharge</strong>. Grain continuity across a long run of slab fronts is typically a paid custom-order upgrade at this price point, or simply not offered. Eclipse builds it in as standard, and it's one of the strongest things to show a client against any competing frameless line at the Eclipse tier.</p>

<p>Market position: <strong>premium semi-custom</strong> — the same tier as Shiloh, built on the same WW Wood quality standard. Best fit: a contemporary kitchen where the homeowner wants European look and European materials without European cost or lead time.</p>
</section>

<section id="construction">
<h2>Construction &amp; specs anatomy</h2>
<p>The honest answer to "is this a real full-access box, or a face-frame box without the frame?" — Eclipse is real full-access, built around frameless geometry from the ground up.</p>

<div class="anatomy-wrap">
<table class="anatomy">
  <tbody>
    <tr><th scope="row">Construction</th><td>Frameless full-access — no face frame. Doors and drawers fully overlay the box, giving the clean continuous front a contemporary kitchen requires.</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Cabinet box</th><td>3/4" particleboard standard. <strong>Plywood upgrade (+10%)</strong> available in most species — plywood core with MDF outer bands for stability; some materials/finishes not compatible with plywood.</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Box panels</th><td>3/4" thick top, bottom, side panels; 3/4" thick adjustable shelving; 3/4" thick hanging rail; 3/4" × 4" stretchers for stability and rigidity.</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Edge banding</th><td>PVC edge banding, color-coordinated to the door material — not always an exact color match, worth setting expectations on with the homeowner.</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Interior color</th><td>Choice of maple print, white, or linen laminate interior (some restrictions by product).</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Drawer box options</th><td>5/8" wood dovetail (standard, $0), 5/8" simulated metal drawerbox (standard, $0), 3/4" wood dovetail with branded Eclipse logo (+$57, or $107 in walnut), Blum LEGRABOX stainless steel (+$372 — full extension included).</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Drawer guides</th><td>Blum TANDEM edge 7/8 extension with BLUMOTION soft-close standard ($0). Full extension (FEG) +$72 — LEGRABOX includes full extension.</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Door hinges</th><td>Blum CLIP top BLUMOTION soft-close, easy adjustment, concealed.</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Interior access</th><td>Up to 10% wider drawer and door openings vs. face-frame at the same outside dimension — a storage win you can actually measure.</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Sizing</th><td>Square cabinet mods up to 6" in H/W/D = 30%; over 6" = 50%; angled mods = 50%. Free width reductions up to 30% of an order. Free depth reductions at 13", 15", 16", 18", 21", 24" base.</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Wall cabinet tops/bottoms</th><td>Standard finished tops and bottoms on wall cabinets (with some product-specific restrictions).</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Open shelving</th><td>Pairs cleanly with the new 1¼" edge-banded plywood floating shelf for open display sections. <a href="/playbook/shiloh-edge-banded-shelf">See spec details</a> — currently spec'd through Shiloh SKUs.</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Showroom merchandising</th><td>Eclipse Merchandiser Display (ECL-M-DISP2 / model 5570) — 64" W × 84" H × 24" D, holds 44 sample doors. <a href="/playbook/eclipse-merchandiser-display">See display spec card</a>.</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Color combinations</th><td>600+ possible material × color combinations across paints, stains, laminates, acrylics, and reconstituted veneers.</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Lead time</th><td>~6 weeks from order acknowledgment — same cycle as Shiloh and Aspect.</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Warranty</th><td>10-year limited warranty.</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Made in</th><td>Dudley, Missouri — W.W. Wood Products.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>

<section id="door-styles">
<h2>Door styles</h2>
<p>Eclipse offers <strong>the same 50+ door styles as Shiloh</strong> (Hanover, Square Flat Panel, Square Raised Panel, Aspen, Heritage, Lancaster, the full Group A and Group B lineup) plus one Eclipse-exclusive: <strong>Metropolitan</strong>, the modern slab door that's the platform for the specialty materials.</p>

<p>The pricing groups carry over from Shiloh: Group A (no upcharge), Group B (+$44/door). The Metropolitan slab is Group A.</p>

<h3>What's special about Metropolitan</h3>
<p>Metropolitan is the only door style that can be ordered in the specialty material library — high-gloss acrylic, matte velvet acrylic, gloss HPL, matte noir HPL (RAUVISIO), wood-grain HPL, TFL, and natural oak/walnut veneers. Other door styles run on the standard wood species in paints or stains.</p>

<p>Edge options on Metropolitan in specialty materials: matching, satin aluminum-look, or brushed aluminum-look. Acrylic versions can also be specified with a 3D edge.</p>
</section>

<section id="gola">
<h2>GOLA handleless system</h2>
<p>Eclipse offers a built-in <strong>GOLA channel handle system</strong> — an integrated aluminum channel routed directly into the cabinet door or drawer front, eliminating the need for external pulls or knobs. The result is a seamless, ultra-modern aesthetic that's become a signature of high-end European kitchen design, available in Eclipse at a domestic price point.</p>

<p>GOLA channels come in multiple profiles and finishes to match any contemporary project. Pair them with Metropolitan slab fronts and the specialty-materials library for a true Euro-modern kitchen that ships in six weeks.</p>

